tourists are evacuating Yosemite  National Park this morning because of  dangerous conditions from a nearby  wildfire the Ferguson fire has burned  about thirty eight thousand acres in  California Sierra Nevada firefighters  battling the flames will work in nearly  100 degree temperatures today Dean  Reynolds is at the USMNT Valley Lodge as  visitors begin to leave Dean good  morning good morning well flames from  the Ferguson fire are getting closer to  where we are but a heavy layer of smoke  has been blanketing the park for much of  the last week and that's affected the  vacation plans of hundreds of thousands  of tourists and forced the closure of  Yosemite Valley for the first time in  nearly 30 years battling steep rugged  terrain and oppressive heat emergency  crews are racing to contain the Ferguson  fire for nearly two weeks flames have  chewed through more than 57 square miles  of forest in the Sierra Nevadas  blanketing nearby Yosemite National Park  in a thick cloud of smoke we're seeing  variable air quality but it's the  sustained exposure that concerns us  those concerns led Park officials to  close the seven and a half mile valley  causing the cancellation of at least a  thousand hotel and lodge reservations  during the peak summer season it just  got to the point the cumulative effect  poor air quality the weather forecast  saying were not looking at any relief  soon the decision gives firefighters  time to perform preventative measures  without interference from tourists many  of whom have had their trips cut short  we're gonna try to get out of here  before the big rush Nancy Devonport came  from Utah she says she's been here for a  week with 24 family members but the  dangerous air forced them to cancel most  of their plans it's not healthy to go on  hikes or any of the tours we couldn't  you know do a lot of the things we  wanted to do now popular sections of the  park will officially closed for the next  four days starting at noon local time  today but this Lodge where we're at  isn't taking any chances and wants all  its guests out  by nine o'clock this morning Gail all  right Dean thank you very much
 

